# Attributes for `git archive`, which is what the release job uses to build the
# source tarball attached to every release. An "upstream source" tarball excludes
# the distro packaging, the same way a project that ships its own tarball does
# not include debian/ or the PKGBUILD inside it: those are added by the packager.
#
# This matters for a reason that is not cosmetic. The PKGBUILD must record the
# sha256 of the tarball its source line points at, and that tarball used to
# contain the PKGBUILD itself, so the checksum could never converge: editing the
# hash changed the tree, which changed the tarball, which changed the hash.
# Excluding packaging/ from the archive makes the hash a function of the tagged
# source only, so it stays valid while packaging files are edited.
/packaging/ export-ignore
/debian/ export-ignore
/.github/ export-ignore
